        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/23/apple-iphone-18-pro-rebooting-bug-software-update-fix/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/09/mayo.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">On Monday, <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/21/iphone-18-pro-face-id-bug-system-reboot/\">we reported on an issue</a> where iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max users were seeing their phone freeze and reboot following a failed Face ID attempt. To us, it appeared to be a software glitch rather than an inherent hardware fault.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Apple has now confirmed to 9to5Mac that a software update to address this problem is in the works, and should be available early next week.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"iphone-18-pro\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1071348\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/23/apple-iphone-18-pro-rebooting-bug-software-update-fix/#more-1071348\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
